WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:01.320
Hello internet!

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.460
You’re watching Mostly Weekly

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.880
and I’m intermittently Andrew Heaton.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.760
Interns!

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.360
The muse of Hollywood studios who like to
ask:

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.060
what if an intern was a hilariously out-of-touch
old dude?

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.680
The answer is hijinx.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.280
This summer millions of students across our
great land are working in internships.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.300
How do I know?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.040
Because we asked our Mostly Weekly intern,
Clint,

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.500
to do some fact-checking and some work around
the set.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.560
And according to his research, the US has
8 bajillion unpaid interns.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.580
So why do people love unpaid interns?

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.940
Because the labor is cheap, if not a bit unreliable.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.500
Fuck!

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.250
We're proud of you Clint! you're doing-

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.400
Shut up!

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.560
Companies want cheap labor

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.720
and college students are willing to work for
the experience.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.700
And job seekers are willing to work for free

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.829
in order to get a foot in the door at a company
they like.

00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:51.580
But many companies are eliminating their unpaid
internship programs altogether.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.100
Why?

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.380
Because most unpaid interns are illegal.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.140
In fact, the exact wording says:

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.880
“The employer that provides training

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:01.820
derives no immediate advantage from the activities
of the intern;

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.220
and on occasion its operations may actually
be impeded.”

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.860
So. in other words, you can hire an unpaid
intern,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.120
you just don’t let them do anything helpfoot.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.170
Clint- I think maybe you misspelled “helpful”
in the teleprompter buddy.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.760
No, Clint, don’t be like that!

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.920
Why you gotta...

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.119
I'll let you come in at ten.

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:22.299
Here's the thing:

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:25.329
I think two consenting adults should be able
to do whatever they want

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:27.380
with or to each other

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.940
and that includes internships.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.260
Unpaid interns meet a network of people

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.380
you could only meet through the wonderful
world of work!

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.080
And finally understand the movie “Office
Space.”

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.040
References.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.960
References are an incredibly valuable way
to find work

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.859
you can only get by having work experience
in the first place.

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:47.490
Back in the days before unpaid internships,

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.709
I used to give my own number as a reference

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:52.200
and pretended to be my own former employer.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.460
Oh ay, Heaton was a great guy.

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:55.329
Eye for detail, all that stuff.

00:01:55.329 --> 00:02:00.020
Uh, knows Microsoft suite and... haggis.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.180
All right, that's the bagpipes, got to go

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.400
Braveheart to you.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.340
Well my word!

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.789
Andy Heaton's a tall drink of water

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:10.060
that never had no drug charges.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.900
Another benefit is work lessons

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.440
Without an unpaid internship, where-

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.680
uh, hey buddy,

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.070
you got your finger on the lens, could you
take, could you move your finger?

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.730
You just moved your fingers up, that's not
doing anything,

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.320
Okay, I'm just going to work around, uh

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:21.920
Work lessons!

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.160
They're important, you can get them from unpaid
internships.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.230
There are also a suspicious number of congressmen

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.410
who have unpaid interns

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.310
but ALSO voted to increase the minimum wage

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:34.220
but ALSO use unpaid interns.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.680
Hey Clint, don't walk in front of the green
screen.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.880
You're not my dad!

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:50.560
So for them, it’s fine to work for $8 an
hour or zero, but nothing in between.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.460
Hashtag: congresslogic.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.620
Look unpaid internships aren’t ideal,

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.380
it’s better to get paid, I know.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.980
But it’s also better than not having any opportunities
at all.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:03.720
Wanting to ban unpaid internships is like
wanting to ban hot pockets

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.420
because we don’t have both hot pockets and
pizza.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.300
And, let’s at least consider things from
the perspective of the employer.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.920
If the government forces an employer to pay
their interns,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.780
what possible incentive do they have to hire
a twenty-something nobody

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.280
for eighty-something days?

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.710
That’s not even enough time to figure out
how to work the fax machine.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.760
Or in Clint’s case- facts.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:24.800
I love ya buddy!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:25.720
Shut up!

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:30.400
Weirdly, working for free can be an advantage
for someone looking to get experience.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.340
But companies face increasing legal scrutiny
to hire them,

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.520
which is why we should legalize unpaid-

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.480
Hello?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.520
Hey Clint, buddy!

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.760
Well, how did you get there?

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.200
I... cut the blue wire?

